/extern/

.venv/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# editor scratch
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Build outputs. Reproducible, so there is nothing to preserve:
#   uv run python tools/build-slides.py <deck>
out/

# Quarto's own cache, and a stray in-place render: `quarto render <file>` writes
# beside the source and ignores output-dir, where a bare `quarto render` does not.
#
# head.html is SOURCE, not output. The globs below exist for stray renders and
# will happily eat a source file that shares their suffix — which is exactly what
# happened to guides.html once, before it became the second half of head.html:
# unnoticed for several commits, because the working tree still had it. Add a
# negation for any new source file whose extension collides.
.quarto/
/demo/*.html
/template/*.html
!/demo/head.html
!/template/head.html
/demo/*.pdf
/template/*.pdf
/demo/*.pptx
/template/*.pptx
/demo/*_files/
/template/*_files/

# Dead ends kept for reference. The README there says how to regenerate them,
# which is worth committing; the artefacts themselves are not.
/trash/*
!/trash/README.md
!/trash/*.py

# Your own decks. The folder is tracked so it is there after a clone; everything
# you put in it is not, so your talks never become part of this repository and
# `git pull` never conflicts with your work.
/talks/*
!/talks/README.md
